    delphi:hasConfidence "0.84"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "The universal prediction has a clear counterexample criterion and broad occurrence and phylogenetic data exist. Taxonomic uncertainty and sampling incompleteness reduce confidence but can be modeled." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Across pairs of regions, quantify counts of close phylogenetic replacements and test whether those counts predict shared species after controlling for area, distance and sampling. A reliably positive association supports the prediction; region pairs with many allied forms but no shared species refute its universal wording." ;
